Aim
To write a Python program using Pandas to create a dataset, identify and handle missing values, clean the data, and perform data exploration using various functions.

Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Pandas library.
3. Create a dictionary containing student names, ages and marks.
4. Convert the dictionary into a Pandas DataFrame.
5. Display the original dataset.
6. Identify and display the missing values using isnull().sum().
7. Replace missing age and marks values with their respective column means using fillna().
8. Display the cleaned dataset.
9. Display the first two rows using head().
10. Display the DataFrame information using info().
11. Display the statistical summary using describe().
12. Display the shape of the DataFrame.
13. Stop the program.

Code

import pandas as pd

# Creating dataset
data = {
    "Name": ["Siya", "Riya", "Priya", "Anu"],
    "Age": [20, 21, None, 19],
    "Marks": [90, 85, 95, None]
}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)
# Display original data
print("Original Data:")
print(df)
# Checking missing values
print("\nMissing Values:")
print(df.isnull().sum())
# Cleaning data
df["Age"] = df["Age"].fillna(df["Age"].mean())
df["Marks"] = df["Marks"].fillna(df["Marks"].mean())
# Display cleaned data
print("\nCleaned Data:")
print(df)
# Exploring data
print("\nFirst 2 Rows:")
print(df.head(2))
print("\nData Information:")
df.info()
print("\nStatistical Summary:")
print(df.describe())
# Checking shape
print("\nShape:", df.shape)

